-- V11-09 (V1.1): sport-specific measures for the 81 active sports whose measures were only generic (quality score, errors, format).
-- Business configuration, not code: each sport gets 3 measures that mean something in its practice (running pace and heart rate stay where they are;
-- here archery arrows and distance, bowling best score, golf strokes and putts, fencing touches, hiking pack weight, rowing split, ...).
-- The new measures take priority 1..n; the previous generic ones are kept after them (priority n+1..), minus duplicates, so nothing already
-- recorded is hidden. Existing sessions are untouched: extras are free JSON keyed by field id.
-- Idempotent (a sport whose first field is already the new one is skipped). The caller owns the transaction: never BEGIN/COMMIT here.
-- Rollback: update public.sports set extra_fields = (select jsonb_agg(f) from jsonb_array_elements(extra_fields) f where (f->>'priority')::int > <n>) for the sports listed in this file.
